Ladybird measures fit-content space around the static-position center
using twice the distance to the nearer containing-block edge. With a
300px containing block and a center at 220px, that space is 160px for
the margin box. Blink computes the same available space through its
ComputeUnclampedIMCBInOneAxis() function.

Gecko retains its hypothetical-position inset calculations through
ReflowInput::InitAbsoluteConstraints(). WebKit retains that path in
PositionedLayoutConstraints::computeStaticPosition(). Neither path
applies this explicit centered-space limit, so Ladybird follows the CSS
Position center-inset rule and Blink’s behavior for this case.

Ladybird’s StaticPosition guard preserves sizing within a grid area.
Blink derives the static position from that area in its grid layout
function, GridLayoutAlgorithm::PlaceOutOfFlowItems(). Gecko selects
StaticPosIsCBOrigin in AbsoluteContainingBlock::ReflowAbsoluteFrame()
for a direct child using a grid-area containing block. WebKit’s
PositionedLayoutConstraints::computeStaticPosition() sets both insets
to zero for that case, preserving the whole area for sizing.
